  "rationale": "Every exfiltration technique needs admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup, and each of those needs a foothold on that host first. The only way to get a foothold is auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup. Because mfa_dbadmin is deployed, these require stolen_dbadmin AND (admin_dc OR admin_adfs). admin_dc needs foothold_dc, and admin_adfs needs foothold_adfs. Those footholds come only from auth_dc and auth_adfs, which both require NOT mfa_admin; mfa_admin is deployed, so both are blocked. The attacker can still reach_internal, phish, kerberoast to get stolen_admin, and leak stolen_dbadmin from the CI server, but cannot get admin_dc or admin_adfs. So no foothold on db, fileserver or backup is possible, and exfiltrated cannot become true."
